# DATABASE DESIGN DOCUMENT (DDD)

# Secure Container Supply Chain Security Platform

Version: 1.0

Database: PostgreSQL 17

ORM: Prisma

Status: Design Approved

---

# 1. Database Overview

The Secure Container Supply Chain Security Platform stores:

* User accounts
* Roles and permissions
* Container images
* Vulnerability scans
* SBOMs
* Security findings
* Compliance reports
* Notifications
* Audit logs

Database Type:

Relational Database

Technology:

PostgreSQL

Design Principles:

* Third Normal Form (3NF)
* Strong Referential Integrity
* ACID Compliance
* Auditability
* Scalability

---

# 2. Entity Relationship Overview

Users
↓
Images
↓
Scans
↓
Vulnerabilities

Images
↓
SBOMs

Users
↓
Reports

Users
↓
Notifications

Users
↓
Audit Logs

---

# 3. User Management Module

## Table: users

Purpose:

Store platform users.

Columns:

id UUID PK

email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL

password_hash TEXT NOT NULL

first_name VARCHAR(100)

last_name VARCHAR(100)

role_id UUID FK

status VARCHAR(20)

last_login TIMESTAMP

created_at TIMESTAMP

updated_at TIMESTAMP

Indexes:

UNIQUE(email)

INDEX(role_id)

Business Rules:

* Email must be unique.
* Password stored using bcrypt.

---

## Table: roles

Purpose:

Store RBAC roles.

Columns:

id UUID PK

name VARCHAR(50)

description TEXT

created_at TIMESTAMP

Sample Values:

* Admin
* Security Analyst
* Developer
* Viewer

---

## Table: permissions

Purpose:

Permission catalog.

Columns:

id UUID PK

name VARCHAR(100)

description TEXT

created_at TIMESTAMP

Examples:

create_scan

delete_scan

generate_report

manage_users

---

## Table: role_permissions

Purpose:

Many-to-many mapping.

Columns:

id UUID PK

role_id UUID FK

permission_id UUID FK

---

# 4. Image Registry Module

## Table: images

Purpose:

Store container images.

Columns:

id UUID PK

name VARCHAR(255)

tag VARCHAR(100)

digest VARCHAR(255)

registry VARCHAR(255)

repository VARCHAR(255)

image_size BIGINT

status VARCHAR(50)

created_by UUID FK

created_at TIMESTAMP

updated_at TIMESTAMP

Example:

nginx:latest

alpine:3.20

Indexes:

INDEX(name)

INDEX(digest)

INDEX(created_by)

---

# 5. Scan Management Module

## Table: scans

Purpose:

Track scan executions.

Columns:

id UUID PK

image_id UUID FK

scan_type VARCHAR(50)

status VARCHAR(50)

started_at TIMESTAMP

completed_at TIMESTAMP

duration_seconds INTEGER

initiated_by UUID FK

created_at TIMESTAMP

Scan Types:

* Vulnerability
* SBOM
* Compliance

Statuses:

* Pending
* Running
* Completed
* Failed

Indexes:

INDEX(image_id)

INDEX(status)

INDEX(started_at)

---

# 6. Vulnerability Module

## Table: vulnerabilities

Purpose:

Store discovered vulnerabilities.

Columns:

id UUID PK

scan_id UUID FK

cve_id VARCHAR(100)

severity VARCHAR(20)

cvss_score DECIMAL(4,2)

package_name VARCHAR(255)

installed_version VARCHAR(100)

fixed_version VARCHAR(100)

description TEXT

published_date TIMESTAMP

created_at TIMESTAMP

Severity Values:

* Critical
* High
* Medium
* Low
* Informational

Indexes:

INDEX(cve_id)

INDEX(severity)

INDEX(package_name)

INDEX(scan_id)

---

# 7. SBOM Module

## Table: sboms

Purpose:

Store generated SBOM metadata.

Columns:

id UUID PK

image_id UUID FK

format VARCHAR(50)

generator VARCHAR(50)

storage_path TEXT

generated_at TIMESTAMP

created_at TIMESTAMP

Formats:

* CycloneDX
* SPDX

Generators:

* Syft
* Trivy

Indexes:

INDEX(image_id)

INDEX(format)

---

# 8. Compliance Module

## Table: compliance_reports

Purpose:

Store compliance assessment results.

Columns:

id UUID PK

scan_id UUID FK

framework VARCHAR(100)

score DECIMAL(5,2)

status VARCHAR(50)

report_path TEXT

generated_at TIMESTAMP

Frameworks:

* CIS Docker Benchmark
* NIST
* OWASP
* ISO27001

Indexes:

INDEX(framework)

INDEX(status)

---

# 9. Reporting Module

## Table: reports

Purpose:

Store generated reports.

Columns:

id UUID PK

report_type VARCHAR(50)

generated_by UUID FK

file_path TEXT

generated_at TIMESTAMP

created_at TIMESTAMP

Report Types:

* Vulnerability
* SBOM
* Compliance
* Executive

Indexes:

INDEX(report_type)

INDEX(generated_by)

---

# 10. Notification Module

## Table: notifications

Purpose:

Store user notifications.

Columns:

id UUID PK

user_id UUID FK

title VARCHAR(255)

message TEXT

type VARCHAR(50)

is_read BOOLEAN

created_at TIMESTAMP

Types:

* Critical Alert
* Scan Complete
* Report Generated

Indexes:

INDEX(user_id)

INDEX(is_read)

---

# 11. Audit Module

## Table: audit_logs

Purpose:

Track all critical actions.

Columns:

id UUID PK

user_id UUID FK

action VARCHAR(255)

resource_type VARCHAR(100)

resource_id UUID

ip_address VARCHAR(100)

user_agent TEXT

created_at TIMESTAMP

Examples:

Login

Logout

Create Scan

Delete Report

Generate SBOM

Indexes:

INDEX(user_id)

INDEX(resource_type)

INDEX(created_at)

---

# 12. Queue Tracking Module

## Table: jobs

Purpose:

Track asynchronous jobs.

Columns:

id UUID PK

job_type VARCHAR(50)

status VARCHAR(50)

payload JSONB

attempts INTEGER

created_at TIMESTAMP

updated_at TIMESTAMP

Job Types:

* Scan Job
* SBOM Job
* Report Job

Statuses:

* Pending
* Running
* Completed
* Failed

Indexes:

INDEX(job_type)

INDEX(status)

---

# 13. Storage Strategy

Database Stores:

* Metadata
* Scan Results
* References

Object Storage Stores:

* SBOM Files
* Reports
* Exported Data

Suggested Storage:

MinIO

Future:

AWS S3

---

# 14. Data Retention Policy

Audit Logs

Retain 365 Days

Notifications

Retain 90 Days

Scan Results

Retain Indefinitely

Reports

Retain 180 Days

SBOM Files

Retain Indefinitely

---

# 15. Backup Strategy

Database Backup

Daily Full Backup

Transaction Logs

Every 15 Minutes

Backup Retention

30 Days

Recovery Objective (RPO)

15 Minutes

Recovery Time Objective (RTO)

1 Hour

---

# 16. Performance Optimization

Connection Pooling

PgBouncer

Query Optimization

Indexes

Partitioning

Audit Logs

Materialized Views

Dashboard Analytics

Caching

Redis

---

# 17. Future Database Enhancements

Multi-Tenant Support

Tenant Table

Tenant Isolation

Soft Deletes

Data Versioning

Historical Scan Snapshots

Advanced Analytics Warehouse

---

# 18. Prisma Entity Order

1. User
2. Role
3. Permission
4. RolePermission
5. Image
6. Scan
7. Vulnerability
8. SBOM
9. ComplianceReport
10. Report
11. Notification
12. AuditLog
13. Job

